<title>RUSSIA: Russia has lifted 5 mln barrels Iraqi oil - importer.</title>
<headline>Russia has lifted 5 mln barrels Iraqi oil - importer.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian companies have lifted around five million barrels of oil from Iraq, or about one fifth of the total envisaged under contracts between Russia and Baghdad, a senior Russian oil executive said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;They (Russian companies) have exported about five million barrels,&quot; said Yuri Agababov, deputy director of Zarubezhneft which is co-ordinating Russian purchases of Iraqi oil.</p>
<p>Zarubezhneft is also one of the Russian companies which has signed contracts to export Iraqi oil.</p>
<p>He said Russian oil companies were buying 140,000 barrels per day (bpd) over six months, or about 25 million barrels in total.</p>
<p>Iraq began exporting oil for the first time in six years in December 1996 under a U.N. deal which allows Baghdad to sell $2 billion worth of crude over six months for food and medicine. It is expected to export about 600,000 bpd.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +095 941 8520</p>
